**3. The One Alternative Worth Understanding: Capital Structure (Round 8 Contestant D)**

This is a completely different philosophy that does not compete with TRIAD-SWEEP on strategy -- it competes on how you define "15% ROI."

Round 8 Contestant D argues: stop trying to make the trading account produce 15% per month. Instead, make the account produce 3-6% per month (which is realistic and safe with a single edge at 0.5% risk), and achieve 15% ROI on your personal capital through prop firm leverage.

The math: if you have $10,000 of personal capital and get a $60,000 prop account, a 4% monthly return on the account is $2,400. After an 80% payout and $300 in fees, that is $1,620 net -- which is 16.2% ROI on your personal $10,000.

This is not a different trading strategy. It is a different financial structure. And it has real risks: prop firms can deny payouts, fail your challenge, change rules, or go bankrupt. But it is the only mathematically honest way to get 15%+ on your money every month without risking account death.

You could combine this with TRIAD-SWEEP: run TRIAD-SWEEP at 0.24% risk on a $150,000 prop account base, producing 9-11% per month on the account. With a 90% payout, that is $12,600-$15,400 per month. Against $10,000 of personal capital (challenge fees), that is 126-154% ROI per month on personal capital. This is the real "out of the box" answer.

