**5. My Final Answer**

No, there is nothing fundamentally better than the TRIAD-SWEEP strategy I shared. The only improvements available are:

1. Add asymmetric runners on GBPJPY and XAUUSD (close 60% at +1R, let 20% run with no target) to boost strong months by 1-3% without adding risk
2. Understand that the most reliable path to 15%+ ROI on your personal money is not making the account produce 15% every month -- it is running a safe 9-11% on the account and using prop firm leverage to amplify the return on your personal capital

The honest ceiling for a single trading account targeting 7-8% maximum drawdown over 10 years is 8-11% average per month. Strong months will reach 13-15%. There will be 1-2 losing months per year. The 10-year survival probability is 35-40% with proper risk management. No strategy in this repository or anywhere else can honestly do better than this without either exceeding the drawdown limit or depending on leverage that introduces its own risks.

